<title>USA: DuPont Merck introduce new dosages of Coumadin.</title>
<headline>DuPont Merck introduce new dosages of Coumadin.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The DuPont Merck Pharmaceutical Co said it introduced two new dosage strengths for its oral anticoagulant, Coumadin.</p>
<p>The new strengths are a 3-mg and a 6-mg tablets available in bottles of either 100 or 1000 tablets.</p>
<p>DuPont Merck is a partnership between DuPont Co and Merck &amp; Co Inc which focuses on the research, development and delivery of pharmaceuticals.</p>
</text>
